<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The American Songbag (Carl Sandburg)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1927</span><span class="sg-chain-h">printed with a piano arrangement by Alfred G. Wathall</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Está Chegando a Hora (Carmen Costa)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1942</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Portuguese version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Teraz jest wojna</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">Second World War</span><span class="sg-chain-h">street chant to the melody in occupied Poland</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Los tres García (film, Pedro Infante)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1947</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">You, Me, and Us (Alma Cogan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1957</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune with English words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Cats and Bruises (Speedy Gonzales cartoon)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">I'm Never Gonna Change (José Feliciano)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording; Grammy for Best Latin Pop Performance</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 6 (Shostakovich), finale</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adaptation used</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Frito Bandito advertisement</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words; criticised as racist</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Oy (Mohsen Namjoo, with Golshifteh Farahani)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">version with Persian poems</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Red Dead Redemption 2</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2018</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Spanish song on the bandits of the Sierra Morena</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">early 17th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the first verse</span></li></ul></section>
